{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "im-cook-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.83: `im-cook` -- inspection and maintenance, as MOVES 5 applies the default database's IMCoverage. THC, CO, NOx and NMHC at running and start exhaust for the motorcycle (11), passenger car (21), passenger truck (31), light commercial truck (32) and single-unit short-haul truck (52), every fuel MOVES adds, in Cook County, Illinois (17031), DEFAULT domain, 2020, August, weekday, hour 7, from the default database alone.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the I/M blend (`rt_imAdjustFract`, `rtMode_imBlendedRate`): baseratecalculator.go:1186-1196 replaces every rate by `(1 - IMAdjustFract) x meanBaseRate + IMAdjustFract x meanBaseRateIM`, where IMAdjustFract is, per (pollutant-process, model year, source type, fuel), the sum over the county's IMCoverage programs of `IMFactor x complianceFactor / 100` (baseratecalculator.go:580-628). Cook's 2020 programs cover 21, 31 and 32 at model years 1996-2016 (test standards 51, compliance 87.6, 86.5 and 81.0 percent) and 52 at 1968-2015 (test standards 11, 93.7 percent), gasoline and E85, at THC, CO and NOx running and start. So the run holds cohorts IN a program (1996-2016 gasoline cars and trucks, 1980-2015 gasoline 52), cohorts of a covered source type OUTSIDE its model-year range (1980-1995 and 2017-2020 of 21, 31, 32; 2016-2020 of 52), uncovered fuels of covered source types (diesel, CNG, electricity), and an uncovered source type (11). IMFactor is 0 at some (model-year group, age group) keys a program's model-year range covers (it is keyed on the I/M model-year group and the AGE group), so the range alone does not decide. NMHC is chained from the blended THC, so it moves with it.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the chain's `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 4 (single-unit short-haul trucks hold up to four bins of a cohort) and `n_physicsRow` 29 from `sampleVehiclePopulation` and `sourceUseTypePhysics` for the five source types.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "inspection-maintenance"
    ]
  },
